{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  skl    skylake        Intel Skylake/Kaby/Coffee Lake client core (this host's i5-9400 is one): AVX2, no AVX-512\n  skx    skylake-x      Intel Skylake-SP/X server core: AVX-512 F/CD/BW/DQ/VL, two 512-bit FMA units (ports 0+1 fused, 5)\n  glc    goldencove     Intel Golden Cove P-core as in Sapphire Rapids: AVX-512 with VBMI, VPOPCNTDQ, BITALG, GFNI\n  rpl    raptorlake     Intel Raptor Lake / Alder Lake P-core (Golden Cove/Raptor Cove): Golden Cove costs, AVX-512 fused off; GFNI, VAES and VPCLMULQDQ on xmm/ymm\n  zen2   znver2         AMD Zen 2 (Ryzen 5 3600, Steam Deck's Custom APU 0932): AVX2, no AVX-512; latencies measured on both machines with x86bench, other columns estimated from Zen 4\n  zen4   znver4         AMD Zen 4: AVX-512 (VBMI, VPOPCNTDQ, BITALG, GFNI) on 256-bit pipes, 512-bit ops double-pumped\n  x86v2  x86-64-v2      generic x86-64-v2 (SSE4.2, POPCNT): the worst of Skylake, Golden Cove and Zen 4 per class\n  x86v3  x86-64-v3      generic x86-64-v3 (AVX2, FMA, BMI1/2, LZCNT, MOVBE): the worst of Skylake, Golden Cove and Zen 4\n  x86v4  x86-64-v4      generic x86-64-v4 (AVX-512 F/BW/CD/DQ/VL): the worst of Skylake-X, Golden Cove and Zen 4\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "x86_models", "ucas": "x86 models", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "x86_models", "models": [{"model": "skl", "alias": "skylake", "description": "Intel Skylake/Kaby/Coffee Lake client core (this host's i5-9400 is one): AVX2, no AVX-512"}, {"model": "skx", "alias": "skylake-x", "description": "Intel Skylake-SP/X server core: AVX-512 F/CD/BW/DQ/VL, two 512-bit FMA units (ports 0+1 fused, 5)"}, {"model": "glc", "alias": "goldencove", "description": "Intel Golden Cove P-core as in Sapphire Rapids: AVX-512 with VBMI, VPOPCNTDQ, BITALG, GFNI"}, {"model": "rpl", "alias": "raptorlake", "description": "Intel Raptor Lake / Alder Lake P-core (Golden Cove/Raptor Cove): Golden Cove costs, AVX-512 fused off; GFNI, VAES and VPCLMULQDQ on xmm/ymm"}, {"model": "zen2", "alias": "znver2", "description": "AMD Zen 2 (Ryzen 5 3600, Steam Deck's Custom APU 0932): AVX2, no AVX-512; latencies measured on both machines with x86bench, other columns estimated from Zen 4"}, {"model": "zen4", "alias": "znver4", "description": "AMD Zen 4: AVX-512 (VBMI, VPOPCNTDQ, BITALG, GFNI) on 256-bit pipes, 512-bit ops double-pumped"}, {"model": "x86v2", "alias": "x86-64-v2", "description": "generic x86-64-v2 (SSE4.2, POPCNT): the worst of Skylake, Golden Cove and Zen 4 per class"}, {"model": "x86v3", "alias": "x86-64-v3", "description": "generic x86-64-v3 (AVX2, FMA, BMI1/2, LZCNT, MOVBE): the worst of Skylake, Golden Cove and Zen 4"}, {"model": "x86v4", "alias": "x86-64-v4", "description": "generic x86-64-v4 (AVX-512 F/BW/CD/DQ/VL): the worst of Skylake-X, Golden Cove and Zen 4"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  skl    skylake        Intel Skylake/Kaby/Coffee Lake client core (this host's i5-9400 is one): AVX2, no AVX-512\n  skx    skylake-x      Intel Skylake-SP/X server core: AVX-512 F/CD/BW/DQ/VL, two 512-bit FMA units (ports 0+1 fused, 5)\n  glc    goldencove     Intel Golden Cove P-core as in Sapphire Rapids: AVX-512 with VBMI, VPOPCNTDQ, BITALG, GFNI\n  rpl    raptorlake     Intel Raptor Lake / Alder Lake P-core (Golden Cove/Raptor Cove): Golden Cove costs, AVX-512 fused off; GFNI, VAES and VPCLMULQDQ on xmm/ymm\n  zen2   znver2         AMD Zen 2 (Ryzen 5 3600, Steam Deck's Custom APU 0932): AVX2, no AVX-512; latencies measured on both machines with x86bench, other columns estimated from Zen 4\n  zen4   znver4         AMD Zen 4: AVX-512 (VBMI, VPOPCNTDQ, BITALG, GFNI) on 256-bit pipes, 512-bit ops double-pumped\n  x86v2  x86-64-v2      generic x86-64-v2 (SSE4.2, POPCNT): the worst of Skylake, Golden Cove and Zen 4 per class\n  x86v3  x86-64-v3      generic x86-64-v3 (AVX2, FMA, BMI1/2, LZCNT, MOVBE): the worst of Skylake, Golden Cove and Zen 4\n  x86v4  x86-64-v4      generic x86-64-v4 (AVX-512 F/BW/CD/DQ/VL): the worst of Skylake-X, Golden Cove and Zen 4\n"}, "isError": false}}
